---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
const rows = [
  { icon: 'bus', t: 'To CascaiShopping (the mall)', x: 'CascaiShopping has its own bus terminal. MobiCascais lines M03 (loop via Torre), M29 (from São João do Estoril train station), M38 (from Estoril train station) and M01 (from Parede) are listed as serving it. PROBABLY TRUE. I could not confirm a numbered line straight from Cascais Terminal (the bus station), so check the MobiCascais app.' },
  { icon: 'bus', t: 'To the hospital (Hospital de Cascais, Dr. José de Almeida)', x: 'M40 starts at Hospital de Cascais and loops through Alcabideche and Malveira da Serra, per its timetable. M31 is listed as Carcavelos train station to Hospital de Cascais via Bicesse. VERIFIED for the line names. I did not confirm a direct line from Cascais Terminal.' },
  { icon: 'bus', t: 'To CUF Cascais', x: 'I could not confirm any line or stop for CUF Cascais from the official pages I could read. Ask at the MobiCascais app or a kiosk.' },
  { icon: 'bus', t: 'To Guincho (the beach)', x: 'M05 (via Quinta da Marinha), M15 (via Areia) and M43 all run from Cascais train station as loops (circular) and are listed as going via or to Guincho. VERIFIED from the MobiCascais line list. I did not read the stop lists.' },
  { icon: 'bus', t: 'To Estoril and the casino', x: 'M06, M07, M11, M12 and M13 run between Cascais Terminal and Estoril train station. VERIFIED for the line list. I could not confirm which stop is nearest the Casino Estoril.' },
  { icon: 'bus', t: 'To Sintra and Cabo da Roca', x: 'Scotturb (the regional bus company) lists lines 403 and 417 as "Cabo da Roca and Cascais", from Sintra train station to Cascais Terminal, every 30 minutes, 7 days a week. REASONABLY TRUE-UNVERIFIED. The source is an undated Scotturb tourist media kit, and I could not open the current timetable. The 417 number also clashes with MobiCascais line M17 (an old number), so confirm on the day.' },
];
---
<section id="cascais-buses" class="visit groc" aria-label="Buses from Cascais Terminal">
  <h2>Buses from Cascais Terminal</h2>
  <p class="muted">From mobi.cascais.pt and scotturb.com. I assumed CascaiShopping, Hospital de Cascais (Dr. José de Almeida) and CUF Cascais. People who live, work or study in Cascais ride the MobiCascais lines (the "M" numbers) free with a Viver Cascais card. Routes and numbers change, so check the app.</p>
  <div class="vs-grid">
    {rows.map(r => (
      <div class="vs-row">
        <div class="vs-lab"><span class="ic"><Icon name={r.icon} /></span><h3>{r.t}</h3></div>
        <div><p>{r.x}</p></div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>
